## Query Builder

This class builds Oracle SQL depending on the watermark type.

```java
package com.example.datareader.reader;

import com.example.datareader.config.TableReaderProperties;

public class QueryBuilder {

    public static String buildQuery(TableReaderProperties table, boolean hasWatermark) {
        String qualifiedTableName = table.getQualifiedTableName();
        String watermarkColumn = table.getWatermarkColumn();

        if (hasWatermark) {
            return """
                SELECT *
                FROM %s
                WHERE %s > ?
                ORDER BY %s
                FETCH FIRST ? ROWS ONLY
                """.formatted(
                    qualifiedTableName,
                    watermarkColumn,
                    watermarkColumn
                );
        }

        return """
            SELECT *
            FROM %s
            ORDER BY %s
            FETCH FIRST ? ROWS ONLY
            """.formatted(
                qualifiedTableName,
                watermarkColumn
            );
    }
}
```

Important: because table names and column names cannot be bound as JDBC parameters, only allow trusted values from configuration. Do not accept table names directly from user input.

