## Scheduler

This runs all configured table readers every polling interval.

```java
package com.example.datareader.reader;

import com.example.datareader.config.ReaderProperties;
import com.example.datareader.config.TableReaderProperties;
import org.springframework.scheduling.annotation.Scheduled;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class TablePollingScheduler {

    private final ReaderProperties readerProperties;
    private final TablePollingService tablePollingService;

    public TablePollingScheduler(
        ReaderProperties readerProperties,
        TablePollingService tablePollingService
    ) {
        this.readerProperties = readerProperties;
        this.tablePollingService = tablePollingService;
    }

    @Scheduled(fixedDelayString = "#{@readerProperties.pollingIntervalMs}")
    public void pollTables() {
        for (TableReaderProperties table : readerProperties.getTables()) {
            if (!table.isEnabled()) {
                continue;
            }

            try {
                tablePollingService.pollTable(table);
            } catch (Exception ex) {
                System.err.println(
                    "Failed to poll table " + table.getQualifiedTableName()
                        + " from database " + table.getDatabase()
                        + ": " + ex.getMessage()
                );

                ex.printStackTrace();
            }
        }
    }
}
```

For the `@Scheduled` expression to work, expose `ReaderProperties` as a bean named `readerProperties`. Spring usually does this automatically when you use `@EnableConfigurationProperties`.

