## Important Issue: Duplicate Watermark Values

If multiple rows can have the same `CREATED_AT`, this query can miss rows:

```sql
WHERE CREATED_AT > :lastWatermark
```

Example:

| ID | CREATED_AT |
|---:|:---|
| 101 | 2026-06-12 10:00:00 |
| 102 | 2026-06-12 10:00:00 |
| 103 | 2026-06-12 10:00:00 |

If only part of this batch is processed, saving `CREATED_AT = 10:00:00` could skip remaining rows with the same timestamp.

A better generic solution is to support a composite watermark:

```text
CREATED_AT + ID
```

Then query like:

```sql
SELECT *
FROM CUSTOMER_EVENTS
WHERE CREATED_AT > ?
   OR (CREATED_AT = ? AND ID > ?)
ORDER BY CREATED_AT, ID
FETCH FIRST ? ROWS ONLY
```

For production, I recommend adding this to your config:

```yaml
reader:
  tables:
    - name: CUSTOMER_EVENTS
      database: customerDb
      schema: CUSTOMER_USER
      watermark-column: CREATED_AT
      tie-breaker-column: ID
      watermark-type: TIMESTAMP
      processor: customerEventProcessor
      enabled: true
```

This gives safer incremental reading.

